## Summary

**Event Load: LIGHT** — calibrated to ~1,400 words with the full section set but a tight, snapshot-style treatment (no scenario analysis).

**The day's story:** An Iran–U.S. pause on strikes sent oil down sharply overnight (WTI -6.71%, Brent -7.55% — largest drops in two months), triggering a broad risk-on move. Futures green across all four indices (NDX +1.39% leading), VIX down to 17.72, gold and Bitcoin both bid on dollar-debasement flows. It's a positioning day into a loaded week: **FOMC Wednesday (July 29)** and Mag-7 earnings.

**Watchlist signal I flagged prominently:** The >3% movers are heavily concentrated in watchlist names — quantum led (QBTS +8.57%, IONQ +4.66%), plus nuclear (CCJ +3.55%), space (RKLB +4.69% on a $266M Space Force Alaska deal), and energy storage. I cross-checked RSI: several are bounces off oversold washouts (IONQ RSI 26, RKLB 31), not fresh uptrends, while defense (LMT RSI 72, RTX 74) is stretched.

